Fixed. Both tests (15 passed) and typecheck pass.

**The bug:** `clampToStorageCap` in `src/resources/storage.ts:25` returned `food: resources.food` unchanged while wood and stone were clamped with `Math.min(…, cap)`. So food bypassed the storage cap entirely and stockpiled unboundedly, while wood and stone correctly stopped at the cap.

**The fix:** `food` is now clamped the same way — `Math.min(resources.food, cap)` — matching wood and stone. Also updated the now-inaccurate BUG docstring and the stale comment in `utilizationOf` that referenced the bug.

Verified: `clampToStorageCap` is the single choke point used by `sim/turn.ts:20` (the only place clamping happens during turns), so capping food there covers every settlement. All 15 tests pass; `tsc --noEmit` is clean.


